<title>UK: Petrol war sends Frost H1 profit diving.</title>
<headline>Petrol war sends Frost H1 profit diving.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.5		    vs 6.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.2		    vs 3.2</p>
<p> Pretax		     3.8		    vs 5.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   242.1		  vs 143.3</p>
<p>NOTE - UK petrol retailer the Frost Group Plc said results were in line with market expectations. An industry restructuring, initiated by Exxon Corp's Esso unit's price watch scheme to keep prices competitive, had hit sales and site profits, Frost said.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 5.69		   vs 5.74</p>
<p> Interest		   1.91 payable	 vs 0.12 payable</p>
<p> Tax charge		 0.49		   vs 1.21</p>
<p> Net taxed		  3.28		   vs 4.41</p>
<p> Profit retained	  0.28		   vs 1.41</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 3, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  n/a</p>
<p> Ex-div date		n/a</p>
<p>Note - British petrol retailer Frost said it would be looking to sell sites which no longer had long-term prospects. But it said it was well positioned relative to the other 20 or so smaller suppliers pitted against &quot;the might of Esso, Shell and BP &quot; in a fight for a place in the market. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
